) is running."]}, "overview": "Mississippi's Senate race remains an uphill climb for Democrats, but it has narrowed enough to draw national attention. Incumbent Republican Cindy Hyde-Smith leads Democrat Scott Colom in the two most recent surveys by four to six points, considerably tighter than the state's roughly eleven-point Republican lean. Only a handful of polls exist, however, and several come from partisan sponsors, so the true gap carries real uncertainty.\n\nColom has raised about $2.4 million and drawn support from Barack Obama, Cory Booker, and Raphael Warnock, while outside groups have spent against Hyde-Smith. She counters with incumbency, a cash-on-hand edge, and her own $4.5 million raised. Expert ratings remain overwhelmingly Solid or Likely Republican, and prediction markets put Democratic chances near ten percent. The state's fundamentals and the weight of outside evidence point to a Republican hold, with a late Democratic surge as the main source of suspense.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0354, "margin": -10.93}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0452, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0338, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0557, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0878, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0513, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.051, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0903, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0567, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0543, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0387, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2